Input:
	Purely text-based:  All commands are typed in from the keyboard.
		Movement could be done using arrow keys or by typing in full
		commands like:
			Walk south.
			Look at the tree.
			Say I like you, John.

	35.  How playable do you think this interface is on a scale of 1 (least
	     playable) to 9 (most playable)?
	36.  On a scale of 1 (least enjoyable) to 9 (most enjoyable), how much
	     do you think you would like a game with this type of interface?
	37.  How many hours in a row do you think you would play a game
	     with this type of interface if there were no time constraints?

	Point-and-click based:  This only works for a graphic based game.  You
		could click on something with the right mouse button and you
		would pick it up.  With the left mouse button you would
		examine it.  With the center mouse button you would move in
		that direction.  There would be no keyboard interface at all.

	38.  How playable do you think this interface is on a scale of 1 (least
	     playable) to 9 (most playable)?
	39.  On a scale of 1 (least enjoyable) to 9 (most enjoyable), how much
	     do you think you would like a game with this type of interface?
	40.  How many hours in a row do you think you would play a game
	     with this type of interface if there were no time constraints?

	Hybrid:  Some sort of combination of the two.  The mouse might be
		used for gross movements and quick actions, but the keyboard
		could be used to type in more elaborate commands, like
		conversations or complex actions.

	41.  How playable do you think this interface is on a scale of 1 (least
